SUMMARY:Christmas in the Park
LOCATION:Moncus Park\, 2913 Johnston St\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:🎄✨THREE NIGHTS. ONE PARK. SO MUCH HOLIDAY CHEER!✨🎄\n\
 nChristmas in the Park\, presented by First Horizon Bank\, is BACK Decembe
 r 18–20 from 6:00-9:00PM each night\, and we’re turning Moncus Park in
 to a holiday wonderland!\n\nGather your friends\, bring the family\, and g
 et ready for a weekend filled with twinkling lights\, live music\, festive
  treats\, and plenty of reasons to make a night of it. Best of all? Admiss
 ion is FREE!\n\n🎅 HERE’S WHAT’S WAITING FOR YOU:\n\n✨ Twinkly lig
 hts throughout the Park\n🎶 Live music all weekend long\n🛍️ Merry M
 arket\, a Christmas market featuring local artisans\n❄️ Sneauxville\, 
 with FREE ice sledding down the hill\n🎁 Santa’s Workshop with crafts 
 from the Children's Museum of Acadiana\n💌 Letters to Santa\n📸 Photos
  with Santa\n🧱 Building Block Zone for creative little builders\n🍫 S
 ’mores\, hot cocoa\, mocktails\, and holiday treats\n🍴 Food Truck All
 ey featuring more than a dozen food trucks\n🚂 Christmas Train rides\n
 🎪 FREE fun jumps\n🫧 Bubble Bus\n🎄 Dedicated Sensory Zone\n\n🎶 
 THE ENTERTAINMENT LINEUP\n\n~ Friday\, December 18: The Skyliners Big Band
  brings the swing with an 18-piece band!\n~ Saturday\, December 19: Corey 
 Ledet & Black Magic take the stage with special guests Gracie Babineaux\, 
 Louie Michot\, Mike Dopsie\, and Nathan Williams.\n~ Sunday\, December 20:
  Enjoy a Christmas movie on the big screen with the Lafayette Shrimpettes 
 and New Natives Brass Band roaming the park!\n\n🚗 PARKING & SHUTTLE INF
 ORMATION 🚎\nAdmission is free for everyone! On-site parking is $20\, wi
 th proceeds supporting Moncus Park’s operations\, maintenance\, and gard
 ens.\n\nPrefer to skip the parking fee? Free parking and shuttle service w
 ill be available at Blackham Coliseum\, located at 2330 Johnston Street. S
 huttles begin at 5 PM each evening and are ADA-friendly.\n\n📍 MONCUS PA
 RK\n2913 Johnston Street\, Lafayette\, LA 70503\n📆 December 18\, 19 & 2
 0\, 6:00-9:00PM each night\n\n🎁 A FEW THINGS TO KNOW\n• The event tak
 es place rain or shine.\n• Wear comfortable shoes and dress in layers fo
 r an evening outdoors.\n• Leave pets at home so they can enjoy a quieter
  night while you enjoy the festivities.\n• Please leave your ice chests 
 at home & support our local vendors & beer tents.\n• No tickets are requ
 ired. Just bring your holiday spirit!\n\n✨ Mark your calendars\, invite 
 your crew\, and get ready for three nights of holiday fun at Moncus Park!\
